Counting with a For loop
Nothing changes as long as all of the variables are updated. I think n is used to represent “number”
(0,5) defines the range of the loop, starting at 0 and stopping before 5
The third number will count by that number, for example if the third number is 2, it will count by 2
Something like (7) is technically (0,7) so it will print from 0 to 6 (7 is exclusive)
It will print the numbers in the range (excluding the second number) and count by 1


print("Type in a message, and I'll display it ten times.")


message = input("Message: ")


for n in range(1,11):
   print(f"{n}. {message}")


print("Type in a message, and I'll display it 6 times.")


message = input("Message: ")


for n in range(2,13,2):
   print(f"{n}. {message}")

